    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 7,
        "sourceEnd": 61,
        "text": "Hi, Tom. Are you working on the city transport report?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "6d7b6b9a61b6d784083e2a71f68e876cc988987aeeec2655ac6a3798ff6e8f11",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 67,
        "sourceEnd": 147,
        "text": "Yes, I am. I'm looking at the numbers for 2010 and 2020. It's quite interesting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "74e1604c75a8ef76dbd5af7ded08e9055a61ef9b2513d3b7e71f7357f3253495",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 155,
        "sourceEnd": 185,
        "text": "Oh, really? What did you find?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "5fa125f7ccd7cbc09c7269af93159514981df2ee6049da57dd3c19a77200eb32",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 191,
        "sourceEnd": 302,
        "text": "Well, in 2010, only 35 percent of people used public transport. But by 2020, that number went up to 55 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "96f3dd2f6a2c855d7a1736eeeded2925729e63e5cae31b550327f89a61879c46",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 310,
        "sourceEnd": 362,
        "text": "That's a big change. Why do you think that happened?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "85e94d0c1eb076e5b240cb94ccbd1c5a8d59a7719a00e0af40f6e3c6fd90912c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 368,
        "sourceEnd": 541,
        "text": "The city invested in new buses and trains. Also, petrol became more expensive. In 2010, petrol was 6 yuan per litre, but in 2020 it was 9 yuan. That's a 50 percent increase.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "c41fd3d48678ae3a95c4774b2ce9b6e6e0b6141bf3a39df63e6eaefd0765d351",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 549,
        "sourceEnd": 582,
        "text": "So driving became more expensive?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "61edfe8cedbfae389c25b9b2bc0def9659e0f9b5d7a9a279d4ea3dd900060684",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 588,
        "sourceEnd": 732,
        "text": "Exactly. And a monthly bus pass cost 100 yuan in 2010, and 150 yuan in 2020. So public transport was still cheaper than driving for many people.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "8235808d6a8449876515b1974b7d8faa4d1779fc6c4f32a3f7fb755926aca2c9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 740,
        "sourceEnd": 788,
        "text": "What about cars? Did the number of cars go down?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "61d021e5d792e510f97b45738b72377ff993e2efcd79e1b5c51bca88ca653fc6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 794,
        "sourceEnd": 935,
        "text": "No, actually it went up. In 2010, there were 100,000 private cars, and in 2020, there were 150,000. So car ownership increased by 50 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "8c31eeccff8183b841300c1a41a4de59fd9655386b32f24bc2d8fc159251e262",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 943,
        "sourceEnd": 1000,
        "text": "That's surprising. I thought fewer people would buy cars.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "a7a6e4e3664554f22f385fa35edf1ff0448afc6c17dff347db5e085f434887e4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 1006,
        "sourceEnd": 1079,
        "text": "Yes, but the city also grew. More people moved to the city, so more cars.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "3cac88c50128c19cc63440679df16660629cc6325a351f1ed9ff5c36cebcf87b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 1087,
        "sourceEnd": 1145,
        "text": "What about cycling? I heard the city built new bike lanes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "bc3165ce2b01445d379f06877e939d16ce83b3d916fe051b6df3faf8c21623cc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 1151,
        "sourceEnd": 1318,
        "text": "Yes, in 2010 there were 20 kilometers of bike lanes, and by 2020 there were 80 kilometers. That's four times as many. The number of cyclists went from 5,000 to 15,000.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "2d7a6fce61db06637281f62668775a61f47528248af8e0468583c4beabe344f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 1326,
        "sourceEnd": 1386,
        "text": "That's good for the environment. But are there any problems?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "f564d6c871ab7037bab5668f5a320766612dee960993a7fc6e5242d07466044c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 1392,
        "sourceEnd": 1539,
        "text": "Well, accidents involving cyclists increased from 50 to 120 per year. So the government is planning to add more lights and signs to improve safety.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "36ce1e25bc2cb9d0b1dcb98705f028147995d30b8b3feb2c13ce2f3d37d30342",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "woman",
        "speaker": "Woman",
        "sourceStart": 1547,
        "sourceEnd": 1609,
        "text": "That sounds like a good plan. Thanks for the information, Tom.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "723a31c63de9ab24127fc12ac1dcbf9ab7905ed484cc086f977275f88ddd75b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "man",
        "speaker": "Man",
        "sourceStart": 1615,
        "sourceEnd": 1667,
        "text": "You're welcome. I'll send you the full report later.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "58d2978670a02cc5df5b17eb1a75036bff511765f34941dc813346fc765b3b7e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
